# Documentation Requirements

After completing a significant piece of work, update the relevant documentation:

## Architecture Decision Records (docs/adr/)
Write a new ADR when you:
- Choose a library, framework, or tool
- Pick an architecture or design pattern
- Make a data model decision
- Change a previous decision

Format: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md` (next sequential number)
Template: Status, Date, Context, Decision, Consequences

## Development Log (docs/devlog/)
Write or update a devlog entry when you:
- Complete a feature or phase
- Finish a significant refactor
- Resolve a complex bug

Format: `docs/devlog/YYYY-MM-DD-short-title.md`
Template: What was done, Key decisions (link ADRs), Issues/Gotchas, Next steps

## Changelog (CHANGELOG.md)
Update the [Unreleased] section when you:
- Add a new user-facing feature (### Added)
- Change existing functionality (### Changed)
- Fix a bug (### Fixed)
- Remove something (### Removed)

Do NOT update documentation for trivial changes (typo fixes, comment updates, etc.)
